{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 154.8, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "Generate complete cached experiment data by running E206 CLI with agency/vehicle_sin modules, or use assessor as evaluation framework for E208 field test (recruit 3-5 small software companies to validate assessment framework).", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "Built Federal Marketplace Assessor prototype (assess.py) - a runnable Python prototype that provides one-command PSC code market assessments for small software teams entering the federal marketplace. Prototype uses cached E206 experiment data (test_7030.json, test_DA10.json) for instant results without API calls. Produces concise one-page reports with verdict, screen score, recipient metrics, software market fit, and recommended entry strategy. Validated across 7030 (PROCEED - best for direct sales) and DA10 (PROCEED - best for GSA Schedule/GWAC pathway). Other codes (7A21, DA01, D304) gracefully degrade when no cached data available. Prototype advances the concrete problem: small software teams have no easy way to assess federal marketplace opportunities. Extends existing E206 integrated CLI analysis into accessible format.", "unlogged_changes": 12}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 18, "session": "2026-10-21-005-finish-federal-marketplace-assessor-prot", "ts": "2026-10-21T05:13:05+00:00"}
